/* Start here entry for function-families (demos/lib/starthere/function-families.js). Generated by tools/activities.py from curriculum/start-here.json:
   edit the data, not this file. demos/lib/starthere.js loads it. */
window.VDStartHere && VDStartHere({"q":"In g(x) = 2 sin(2x − π/2), how far to the right is sin x moved: π/2 or π/4?","q_es":"En g(x) = 2 sen(2x − π/2), ¿cuánto se mueve sen x a la derecha: π/2 o π/4?","setup":"set=sa~2!sb~2!sc~0.79!sd~0!labBlind~0!g%3AmodeSeg~transform!g%3Apresets~sine","do":"<b>sin x: amplitude, period, phase</b>. Predict the shift first. Then read <b>c</b> and the formula for <b>g(x)</b> in the readouts, and follow the orange dot on the peak of sin x to the teal dot on g: <b>Point on f</b> and <b>Lands on g at</b>.","do_es":"<b>sen x: amplitud, periodo, fase</b>. Primero predice el desplazamiento. Luego lee <b>c</b> y la fórmula de <b>g(x)</b> en las lecturas, y sigue el punto naranja en el pico de sen x hasta el punto verde azulado en g: <b>Punto sobre f</b> y <b>Cae sobre g en</b>.","see":"c = 0.7854, which is π/4: the graph is moved right by 0.7854, not by π/2. The demo writes g(x) = 2 sin(2(x − 0.78539816)), which multiplies out to 2 sin(2x − π/2). The peak of sin x at (1.571, 1) lands on g at (1.571, 2): x goes to c + x/b = π/4 + (π/2)/2 = π/2. To read a shift, factor b out of the inside first, because b squeezes the shift along with everything else.","see_es":"c = 0.7854, que es π/4: la gráfica se mueve 0.7854 a la derecha, no π/2. El demo escribe g(x) = 2 sin(2(x − 0.78539816)), que al multiplicar da 2 sen(2x − π/2). El pico de sen x en (1.571, 1) cae sobre g en (1.571, 2): x pasa a c + x/b = π/4 + (π/2)/2 = π/2. Para leer un desplazamiento, primero factoriza b del interior, porque b también comprime el desplazamiento junto con todo lo demás.","explore":[{"setup":"set=sa~3!sb~3.14!sc~0.33!sd~0!labBlind~0!g%3AmodeSeg~transform!g%3Apresets~shm","do":"<b>Oscillation: x = A cos(ωt + φ)</b>: cos t with a = A = 3 cm, b = ω = π rad/s and c = 1/3 s. Read <b>Lands on g at</b>, <b>Period T = 2π/|ω|</b> and <b>Phase φ = −ωc</b>.","do_es":"<b>Oscilación: x = A cos(ωt + φ)</b>: cos t con a = A = 3 cm, b = ω = π rad/s y c = 1/3 s. Lee <b>Cae sobre g en</b>, <b>Periodo T = 2π/|ω|</b> y <b>Fase φ = −ωc</b>.","see":"The first peak of cos t, at (0, 1), lands at (0.3333, 3): the delay is c = 1/3 s, and the period is 2 s. The phase is φ = −ωc = −1.047 rad, which is −π/3. In x = 3 cos(πt − π/3) the π/3 is an angle, not a time: divide it by ω to get the delay.","see_es":"El primer pico de cos t, en (0, 1), cae en (0.3333, 3): el retraso es c = 1/3 s, y el periodo es 2 s. La fase es φ = −ωc = −1.047 rad, que es −π/3. En x = 3 cos(πt − π/3) el π/3 es un ángulo, no un tiempo: divídelo entre ω para obtener el retraso."},{"setup":"set=x0Slide~833!showTan~1!labBlind~0!g%3AmodeSeg~inverse!g%3Apresets~cubic","do":"<b>x³ + x: slope becomes 1/slope</b>, in Inverse mode. Read <b>Slope of f at P</b> and <b>Slope of f⁻¹ at Q, measured</b>, then drag <b>Point x₀</b> and watch both.","do_es":"<b>x³ + x: la pendiente se vuelve 1/pendiente</b>, en el modo Inversa. Lee <b>Pendiente de f en P</b> y <b>Pendiente de f⁻¹ en Q, medida</b>, luego arrastra <b>Punto x₀</b> y observa las dos.","see":"At P = (1, 2) the slope of f is 4, and at the mirrored point Q = (2, 1) the measured slope of the inverse is 0.25, which is 1/4. No formula gives f⁻¹ here (the demo finds it by bisection), yet its slope is always 1/f′(f⁻¹(y)): reflecting in y = x swaps rise and run.","see_es":"En P = (1, 2) la pendiente de f es 4, y en el punto reflejado Q = (2, 1) la pendiente medida de la inversa es 0.25, que es 1/4. Aquí ninguna fórmula da f⁻¹ (el demo la encuentra por bisección), y aun así su pendiente siempre es 1/f′(f⁻¹(y)): reflejar en y = x intercambia la subida y el avance."},{"setup":"set=x0Slide~875!showTan~1!labBlind~0!g%3AmodeSeg~inverse!g%3Apresets~fail","do":"<b>x² on [−2, 2]: not one to one</b>. Read <b>One to one?</b>, then type 0 in the <b>From</b> box of the domain.","do_es":"<b>x² en [−2, 2]: no es uno a uno</b>. Lee <b>¿Uno a uno?</b>, luego escribe 0 en el cuadro <b>De</b> del dominio.","see":"No: f(−0.5) = f(0.5) = 0.25, so a horizontal line meets f twice, and the mirror image fails the vertical line test: it is not a function. With the domain from 0 to 2, x² rises across the whole domain and the inverse is √x. At P = (1.5, 2.25) the slope 3 becomes 1/3 (0.333333) at Q.","see_es":"No: f(−0.5) = f(0.5) = 0.25, así que una recta horizontal corta a f dos veces, y la imagen reflejada no pasa la prueba de la recta vertical: no es una función. Con el dominio de 0 a 2, x² sube en todo el dominio y la inversa es √x. En P = (1.5, 2.25) la pendiente 3 se vuelve 1/3 (0.333333) en Q."}]});
